COMMAND: python3 -c 'import subprocess,time,statistics; hosts=("redis-cache.internal","redis-new.internal");
for h in hosts:
 xs=[]
 for _ in range(100):
  t=time.perf_counter(); r=subprocess.run(["redis-cli","-h",h,"-p","6379","PING"],stdout=subprocess.DEVNULL,stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL,timeout=1); xs.append((time.perf_counter()-t)*1000)
  if r.returncode: break
  time.sleep(.01)
 print(f"{h}: n={len(xs)} p95={statistics.quantiles(xs,n=20)[18]:.2f}ms max={max(xs):.2f}ms failures={100-len(xs)}")'
REASON: Measure current source and target p95 latency and confirm both endpoints remain reachable before changing the application configuration.
